WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:01.650
I found this thing.

00:00:01.650 --> 00:00:05.010
And when I moved
outwards, and breathed.

00:00:05.010 --> 00:00:11.520
[MUTTERING]

00:00:11.520 --> 00:00:13.957
Every time I did that, I was
centered in the character

00:00:13.957 --> 00:00:15.540
and I knew what I
was doing and I knew

00:00:15.540 --> 00:00:19.180
where I was and I was moved.

00:00:19.180 --> 00:00:22.780
I'm going to give you the
actor director's perspective,

00:00:22.780 --> 00:00:27.750
applying my 50 years in the
film industry to your movies.

00:00:27.750 --> 00:00:29.850
You're going to experience
the way that I like

00:00:29.850 --> 00:00:31.020
to work with a screenwriter.

00:00:31.020 --> 00:00:33.270
So I reached out to my
good friend Scott Frank,

00:00:33.270 --> 00:00:35.497
and we will be
looking at character.

00:00:35.497 --> 00:00:37.830
We'll be looking at structure,
we'll be looking at tone.

00:00:37.830 --> 00:00:41.085
I really love how you just
smashed into that flashback.

00:00:41.085 --> 00:00:42.030
It feels right.

00:00:42.030 --> 00:00:44.490
There's a lot of lines that
you could do with looks.

00:00:44.490 --> 00:00:44.990
Right.

00:00:44.990 --> 00:00:47.750
The second line to the bottom,
I would add for f**** sake

00:00:47.750 --> 00:00:49.545
to give her a little attitude.

00:00:53.010 --> 00:00:54.760
When you act and direct
at the same time,

00:00:54.760 --> 00:00:57.130
it's a balancing act.

00:00:57.130 --> 00:00:59.920
Actors tend to
focus on the moment,

00:00:59.920 --> 00:01:02.060
but directors have
to do more than that.

00:01:02.060 --> 00:01:02.560
Action.

00:01:02.560 --> 00:01:04.510
The director is the leader.

00:01:04.510 --> 00:01:06.640
You're never going to
know every single thing

00:01:06.640 --> 00:01:08.110
that your crew member knows.

00:01:08.110 --> 00:01:13.680
But what you do have to have is
a unifying language of vision.

00:01:13.680 --> 00:01:16.080
As a leader, you have
to make a decision,

00:01:16.080 --> 00:01:18.360
and then support that decision.

00:01:18.360 --> 00:01:19.320
Good. cut.

00:01:19.320 --> 00:01:21.510
But it's important that
you know that you're going

00:01:21.510 --> 00:01:22.919
to be filled with anxiety.

00:01:22.919 --> 00:01:24.210
What is this movie going to be?

00:01:24.210 --> 00:01:25.440
How should I redo the script?

00:01:25.440 --> 00:01:27.210
Is it going to be OK?

00:01:27.210 --> 00:01:31.370
You have to learn to trust
that you will be inspired.

00:01:31.370 --> 00:01:34.220
And what I've come to learn
is that eventually, I'll

00:01:34.220 --> 00:01:37.460
be standing there
and it will come.

00:01:37.460 --> 00:01:41.601
That's something that
took a long time to learn.

00:01:41.601 --> 00:01:43.850
The truth is, is that
everything that you have to know

00:01:43.850 --> 00:01:46.370
is inside of you.

00:01:46.370 --> 00:01:48.410
Every decision-making
process is instinctual.

00:01:48.410 --> 00:01:52.132
It can come from
within, and as long

00:01:52.132 --> 00:01:54.090
as you have a pen and a
paper to write it down,

00:01:54.090 --> 00:01:55.840
you're in good shape.

00:01:55.840 --> 00:02:00.670
I'm Jodie Foster, and
this is my MasterClass.

